  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35734478",
      "title": "React Projects - Requirements",
      "sourceHash": "f237cf39f993dce045eeafaacd9ab143488b7ff39044469f9af00cd83751e0ba",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 4.83,
          "en": "So let's get started with React, then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.83,
          "end": 7.35,
          "en": "And to get started, we first of all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.35,
          "end": 9.99,
          "en": "must create a React project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.99,
          "end": 12.713,
          "en": "Now, when working with Vanilla JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.713,
          "end": 15.66,
          "en": "creating a project is as simple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.66,
          "end": 18.96,
          "en": "as creating a new folder, and adding a bunch of HTML,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.96,
          "end": 21.72,
          "en": "JavaScript, and CSS files in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.72,
          "end": 25.92,
          "en": "Now, when building a React web application, a React website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.92,
          "end": 28.17,
          "en": "it's not that simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.17,
          "end": 30.337,
          "en": "Instead, you need a project that performs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.337,
          "end": 32.625,
          "en": "various behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.625,
          "end": 35.73,
          "en": "code transformations automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.73,
          "end": 37.59,
          "en": "And, you typically also want to have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.59,
          "end": 38.841,
          "en": "a nice developer experience",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.841,
          "end": 41.336,
          "en": "where the React app you're working on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.336,
          "end": 44.79,
          "en": "is previewed and automatically updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.79,
          "end": 47.46,
          "en": "whenever you change the React code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.46,
          "end": 50.513,
          "en": "Now, the behind the scenes code transformations are needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.513,
          "end": 52.974,
          "en": "because, as I mentioned before already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 52.974,
          "end": 55.35,
          "en": "when building React apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.35,
          "end": 59.46,
          "en": "you typically blend HTML and JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.46,
          "end": 62.73,
          "en": "in one of the same JavaScript file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.73,
          "end": 66.69,
          "en": "Now, technically this is not valid JavaScript code, though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.69,
          "end": 69.93,
          "en": "The browser would not be able to execute this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.93,
          "end": 71.19,
          "en": "and we will of course learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.19,
          "end": 74.78999999999999,
          "en": "why we're blending the code like this in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 74.78999999999999,
          "end": 77.76,
          "en": "But it is important to understand right now already",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.76,
          "end": 81.51,
          "en": "that this code would not run like this in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.51,
          "end": 84.82900000000001,
          "en": "That's why it must be transformed, compiled, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 84.82900000000001,
          "end": 88.59,
          "en": "to some valid client side JavaScript code that's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.59,
          "end": 91.26,
          "en": "supported by the browser first,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.26,
          "end": 93.53999999999999,
          "en": "so that we as a developer have the convenience",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.53999999999999,
          "end": 96.53999999999999,
          "en": "of mixing HTML and JavaScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.53999999999999,
          "end": 98.61,
          "en": "And as an output, we still get code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 98.61,
          "end": 101.00999999999999,
          "en": "that's supported by the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.00999999999999,
          "end": 102.96000000000001,
          "en": "And that's why we need a project set-up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 102.96000000000001,
          "end": 104.82300000000001,
          "en": "that comes with some built-in tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 104.82300000000001,
          "end": 108.33,
          "en": "that give us this live preview",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 108.33,
          "end": 110.668,
          "en": "with the order reloading up on code changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 110.668,
          "end": 114.261,
          "en": "and where we also get our code transformed under the hood,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 114.261,
          "end": 117.00200000000001,
          "en": "so that once we're done building our reactive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 117.00200000000001,
          "end": 119.88,
          "en": "we get a website that can be deployed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 119.88,
          "end": 123.21,
          "en": "on some hosting providers, and that can then be visited",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 123.21,
          "end": 127.743,
          "en": "and be viewed correctly by visitors from all over the world.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}